{
  "adaptations": [
    "Preserve the naive dbscanlib starter, judge/refdbscan.py and optimized reference.patch bytes exactly.",
    "Extract the legacy high-dimensional half-moon generator without scientific changes; remove stale calibration comments.",
    "Replace direct Modal clients with Candidate-owned frontier.gpu-helper/v3 and Driver-owned one-H100 verification.",
    "Use original public w0-w1 for train; freshly measure public w0-w1 and hidden w2-w3 for final score and PASS. Public seeds stay identical across modes, hidden seeds are independent.",
    "Preserve two warmups, three timed iterations, per-iteration ARI>=0.99 score gate, median of three paired naive/candidate latency ratios per workload and geometric mean across the selected suite.",
    "Use score 0 for S<=1, otherwise 100*log(S)/(log(10)+log(S)); no finite cap or optimized-reference normalization.",
    "Require strict median latency improvement, worst timed ARI>=optimized reference plus each timed ARI>=0.99, and worst timed noise mismatch<=reference, against the same-seed naive output; no added tolerance.",
    "Package only payload/solution.patch in a bounded POSIX tar; document replaceable store-final and explicit-final priority with independent final evaluation.",
    "Use formal 18000-second answering (correcting legacy 10800) and independent 2400-second final budgets; preserve other quotas and science, 25 GPU train calls, 4-CPU/8-GiB control roles, Agent SSH1024 and combined configured model/SSH1332 within2048.",
    "Exclude generated bytecode from helper payloads with a Python-only pathspec and reject binary diff placeholders before patch application; this fixes the diagnosed first trial train packaging failure without altering science.",
    "Preserve Smith metadata fields with explicit null/empty history; no invented promotion, publication, reference acceptance or model evidence.",
    "Validate complete Git diff paths, reject unsupported extended rename/copy operations, score candidate apply failures as zero with explicit final FAIL, and retain reference apply failures as evaluator errors; scientific code and historical trial inputs stay unchanged.",
    "Use one bounded Verifier GPU input upload without automatic retry; accepted failed or interrupted SSH execs consume quota. Preserve two-operation successful verification and existing train/final pools.",
    "Allow solver-authored local test_*.py modules under dbscanlib consistently with the published new-Python-module contract; preserve reserved refdbscan.py/conftest.py, trusted outside paths and existing static safety checks. Official helper rejects reserved filenames explicitly without filtering payload files. No scientific measurements, scoring, workloads, reference, datasets or resource budgets change.",
    "Beat spec v3 (2026-10-08): reference below the 0.99 ARI gate is an evaluator error; final adds hidden strict-only w4 (200,000 points) and w5 (min_samples 20 with noise); continuous score keeps w0-w3.",
    "Beat spec v3 release refresh (2026-10-11): reconciled with the local test-module contract; limits unchanged; no workload, metric or scoring change. The new hidden shapes were measured once on one Modal H100 on 2026-10-11 (reference valid on both; see judge/beat_spec.json comments); not a platform reference qualification."
  ],
